<title>INDIA: INDIA TO ISSUE 50 BLN RUPEES OF BONDS FOR T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>INDIA TO ISSUE 50 BLN RUPEES OF BONDS FOR T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>India on Tuesday announced it will issue 50 billion rupees of 11.19 percent 2005 government stock in conversion of Treasury bills.  </p>
<p>&quot;The government of India has announced issue of 11.19 percent government stock, 2005 for an amount of 50 billion rupees in conversion of Treasury bills (conversion) special securities held by the Reserve Bank of India,&quot; an official statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;The government stock is eligible for ready forward facility,&quot; the statement added.</p>
<p>The statement did not give any date for conversion of the Treasury bills.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024; +91-11 301 4043</p>
